body:
[Proposition lem:rho-closed of arXiv:2609.02544, 'A finiteness theorem for geodesic Leech wheels'] Let $w\ge10$ and set
\[
  \lambda_w=\frac{14(w-1)}{36w-25}.
\]
Then $\ell=\mu(w)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
  (1+\lambda_w^2)\ell^2-(5+\lambda_w)\ell+6-4w\le0.
\end{equation}
Relaxing $\lambda_w\ge\tfrac38$ in (equation eq:rho-sharp of the paper) gives
\begin{equation}
  73\ell^2-344\ell+384-256w\le0,
\end{equation}
and hence the closed form
\begin{equation}
  \mu(w)<\frac{15}{8}\sqrt w+\frac{12}{5}.
\end{equation}
Moreover (equation eq:rho-closed of the paper) holds for every $w\ge1$.

[Proposition 8 of arXiv:2608.04644, 'Khinchin's and Chung's Laws of the Iterated Logarithm at Time Zero for the Linear Stochast'] Recall that $H$ is defined in \eqref{def:H}. Suppose that  Condition \ref{hypo}  holds  and that $H<1$. Then there exists a constant
$c_{2,1}:=\max\left\{C_{1/2,1}, 2^{H+1}\textcolor{black}{\widetilde{\kappa}}\right\}>0$ such that, for all $t\ge s\ge0$ and $x\in\mathbb{R}^d$,
\begin{equation}
	\|u(t,x)-u(s,x)\|_{L^2(\Omega)}
	\le c_{2,1} |t-s|^H.
\end{equation}

