[Prop Sgn-irred of arXiv:2609.00672, 'Deciding superellipticity and computing the Weierstrass normal form'] Let $g\ge 2$ and $n\ge 2$ with $\mathcal S_{g,n}\ne\emptyset$, and put $m=m(g,n)$. Then

\begin{equation}
\mathcal S_{g,n}=\mathcal M(g,C_n,\mathbf C_{g,n}),
\end{equation}

and $\mathcal S_{g,n}$ is irreducible of dimension

\begin{equation}
\dim\mathcal S_{g,n}=
\begin{cases}
m-3, & n\mid m,\\
m-2, & n\nmid m.
\end{cases}
\end{equation}

