[Lemma 21 of arXiv:2606.07096, 'Non-Selection of Lagrangian Trajectories in the Zero-Noise Limit for a Class of Stochastic'] Let $(P_t)_{t\geq 0}$ be the Markov semigroup associated to a Lévy process $L$; assume that there exists $M>0$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \| D P_t f\|_{C^0(\R^d)} \leq M t^{-\frac{1}{\beta}} \| f\|_{C^0(\R^d)}\quad\forall\, t\in (0,1],\quad \forall\,f \in C^0(\R^d).
    \end{equation}
    Then for any $s_1,s_2\in\R$ with $s_1<s_2$ there exists a constant $C=C(s_1,s_2,M)$ such that
    \begin{equation}
        \|  P_t f\|_{B^{s_2}_{\infty,1}} \leq C t^{-\frac{s_2-s_1}{\beta}} \| f\|_{B^{s_1}_{\infty,\infty}}\quad\forall\, t\in (0,1], \quad \forall\,f \in B^{s_1}_{\infty,\infty}(\R^d).
    \end{equation}

