body:
[Theorem 6 (Exact Skellam regimes) of arXiv:2609.02590, 'Directional Optimal Sub-Gamma Scales for Infinitely Divisible Laws'] For the centered Skellam law \eqref{eq:centered-skellam}, the right scale has
the following regimes:
\begin{equation}
 \cplus(X_{\lambda,p})=
 \begin{cases}
  0,&p=0,\\
  \displaystyle\max_{t>0}\Psi_p(t),&0<p<p_+,\\
  \displaystyle\frac{2p-1}{3},&p_+\leq p\leq1.
 \end{cases}

\end{equation}
For $0<p<p_+$, the maximum is attained at a positive finite argument and is
strictly larger than $\max\{0,(2p-1)/3\}$. No uniqueness is asserted. The left
scale is
\begin{equation}
 \cminus(X_{\lambda,p})=
 \begin{cases}
  \displaystyle\frac{1-2p}{3},&0\leq p\leq p_-,\\
  \displaystyle\max_{t>0}\Psi_{1-p}(t),&p_-<p<1,\\
  0,&p=1,
 \end{cases}

\end{equation}
and the middle regime is again interior controlled.

[Lemma 59 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Assume the notation from Definition \ref{Def.ParametersEdge}. Then,
\begin{equation}
\SFb(\zc(\kappa);\kappa) - \SFb(c;\kappa) < 0 \mbox{ and }\SFt(\zc(\kappa);\kappa) - \SFt(c;\kappa) > 0. 
\end{equation}

[Theorem 19 of arXiv:2604.00882, 'On some extensions of generalized counting processes'] Assume the individual claim sizes $Z$ follow the  gamma distribution with shape parameter $r > 0$ and scale parameter $\alpha > 0$. Then  the non-ruin probability is given by:
	\begin{equation}
		\phi(u) = \phi(0)+ e^{-\alpha u} \phi(0) \left\{ e^{\alpha u} \ast \sum_{n=1}^{\infty} \left( \frac{\Lambda}{c} \right)^n \left[ e^{\alpha u} - \frac{1}{\Lambda} \sum_{j=1}^k \lambda_j (\alpha u)^{jr} E_{1,1+jr}(\alpha u) \right]^{\ast n} \right\},
	\end{equation}
	for any $u > 0$, where $\ast$ denotes the convolution operator, $f^{\ast n}$ denotes the $n$-fold convolution power, and $E_{\alpha,\beta}(z)$ is the two-parameter Mittag-Leffler function.

