[Lemma 18 (Dyadic--close harmonic envelope) of arXiv:2609.01570, 'A Proof of Fraenkel's Conjecture'] Let
\[
 H_y^{\rm good}:=\frac1y+
 \sum_{\substack{b\in A\setminus\{1,y\}\\ b\text{ is good}}}
 \frac1{\normQ{yb^{-1}}};
\]
thus the superscript includes the anchor \(b=1\) as well as every selected
good element other than \(y\).  This contribution to the \(y\)-row satisfies
\begin{equation}
 H_y^{\rm good}
 <\frac2m+\frac{10J}{3y}+\frac{2\Harm_{y-1}}{y-1}.
\end{equation}

[Prop proposition:ManyToOneL* of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix $r\geq 0$.  For every non-negative measurable function $\Phi$ on $\mathcal{M}^2_f(\mathbb{R}_+) \times \mathcal{W}_{\overline{E}}$, we have:
\begin{align}
     &  \mathbf{N}^{\bullet, L}_{x,r} \big(  \Phi\big( \rho_U,\eta_U, \overline{W}_U\big)  \big)  
  =   E^0 \otimes \mathcal{N}_{x,r} \Big(  \exp\big(- \alpha\cdot  \uptau \big)\Phi\big( \mathcal{J}_{\uptau}, \widecheck{\mathcal{J}}_{\uptau}, (\bar{\xi}_t:~t\in [0,\uptau] ) \big) \Big). 
\end{align}
Under $\mathbf{N}_{x,r}^{\bullet, L}$, conditionally on $(\rho_U,\eta_U, \overline{W}_U)$ the
processes $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\leftarrow}$ and  $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\rightarrow}$ are independent and their  conditional distributions are as follows:
\begin{itemize}
\item the process $(\rho,\overline{W})^{U,\leftarrow}$ is distributed as  $(\eta, \overline{W})$ under $\mathbb{P}_{\eta_U, \rho_U,\overline{W}_U}^\dagger$; 
\item the process $(\rho, \overline{W})^{U,\rightarrow}$ is distributed as  $(\rho, \overline{W})$ under $\mathbb{P}_{\rho_U,\overline{W}_U}^\dagger$.
\end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

