    & \le C \kappa^{-p}  \sum_{N \in \N_0} \eps_{NT}^{p/2} <\infty.
    \end{align*}
    Thus, we get by the Borel-Cantelli lemma that
\begin{align*}
    \P\left( \limsup_{N \to \infty}\sup_{t \in [NT,(N+2)T]} |X_t- \mathbf{x}_{t-NT}(X_{NT})| > \kappa \right) = 0.
\end{align*}
Since $\kappa$ can be chosen arbitrarily ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:6b78eb24b2d20d690cd7e02b14e3077090f7c2e64d78f0407cc2e236e218ccbc","revision_digest":"sha256:98b18e70012e4bb88eb2264b3e426940c8b51829ee87ce000708d202648564e3","source_id":"arxiv:2608.23462","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

