body:
[Lemma 10 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] Let $\eta$ be a Poisson point process on $(0,1)$ with intensity $x^{-1}\,dx$, and let
\begin{align*}
T(\eta):=\int_{(0,1)}x\,\eta(dx).
\end{align*}
Then
\begin{align*}
\mathcal L\big(\mathfrak q(\eta)\mid T(\eta)\le 1\big)
=
\mathfrak A[\theta_{\mathcal S}],
\end{align*}
where $\theta_{\mathcal S}$ denotes the law on $\mathcal S$ obtained by arranging a $PD(1)$ mass partition in decreasing order. Equivalently,
\begin{align*}
\mathfrak q(\eta)\mid \{T(\eta)\le1\}
\overset{Law}{=}
U(P_1,P_2,\dots),
\end{align*}
where $(P_1,P_2,\dots)$ has distribution $PD(1)$, $U$ is uniformly distributed on $(0,1)$, and $U$ is independent of $(P_1,P_2,\dots)$.

