[Lemma 20 of arXiv:2606.03534, 'Construction and simulation of a path-valued model of dendrite development'] When $\ell_t$ is a Brownian motion absorbed at $\ell=0$ we have 
    \begin{align*}
        \gamma_t^\ell(dp,dq) &= \frac{2(\ell+q-2p)}{\sqrt{2\pi t^3}} \, \exp\bigg( -\frac{(\ell+q-2p)^2}{2t}\bigg) \, \mathds{1}_{\{ 0 < p < \ell\wedge q \}}\,dp \, dq \, \\
        &\quad + 2\bigg(1 - \Phi\left(\frac{\ell}{\sqrt{t}}\right)\bigg) \delta_{(0,0)}(dp,dq) \,.
    \end{align*}

