[Definition 32 of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] A function $\bar\xi:\R^\D_+\to\R$ is called a \textbf{regularization} of $\xi:\R^\D\to\R$ if the following conditions hold.
\begin{enumerate}
    \item  The function $\bar\xi$ agrees with $\xi$ on the intersection of $\R^\D_+$ with the closed unit ball in $\R^\D$.
    \item  The function $\bar\xi$ is Lipschitz and \textbf{proper} in the following sense: $\bar\xi$ is $\R^\D_+$-increasing and, for every $b\in\R^\D_+$, the map $\R^\D_+\ni a\mapsto \bar\xi(a+b)-\bar\xi(a)$ is also $\R^\D_+$-increasing.
\end{enumerate}

[Proposition prop:lower of arXiv:2607.06249, 'Extreme least singular values of Gaussian row submatrices and a phase retrieval stability '] Under the assumptions of Theorem (thm:general of the paper), for every fixed $\varepsilon>0$,
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}\left\{M_m^\mathbb{F}(A_m)\le \exp\left[-\left(\frac{h(\gamma)}{d_\mathbb{F}}+\varepsilon\right)m\right]\right\}\to0.
\end{equation}
If $N_m=\gamma m+O(1)$, the probability in (equation eq:lower-prob of the paper) is bounded by
$C_{\gamma,\varepsilon,\mathbb{F}}m^{1+d_\mathbb{F}/2}e^{-d_\mathbb{F}\varepsilon m}$ for all large $m$.

[Lemma lem:linear of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] For $\mathbf{W}_1, \mathbf{W}_2 \in \mathcal{W}_N$, we have
\begin{equation}
    \mu_N \mleft[ \widetilde{\mathbf{W}_1 \wedge \mathbf{W}_2} \mright] \cdot \mu_N \mleft[ \widetilde{\mathbf{W}_1 \vee \mathbf{W}_2} \mright]
    = \mu_N \mleft[\widetilde{\mathbf{W}}_1\mright] \cdot \mu_N \mleft[\widetilde{\mathbf{W}}_2\mright],
\end{equation}

