body:
[Lemma 31 of arXiv:2608.30668, 'Recurrence and capacity of stable branching random walks'] Consider \(f,g: \Z^d \to \R_+\) and \(\lVert \cdot \rVert\) an Euclidian
norm on \(\R^d\). Assume that
\(f(x)\sim \Vert x\Vert^{-a} \tilde f(\Vert x\Vert)\) and
\(g(x)\sim \Vert x\Vert^{-b} \tilde g(\Vert x\Vert)\) when
\(\Vert x\Vert\to+\infty\), where \(\tilde f, \tilde g\) are slowly
varying functions and \(a,b >0\) satisfy \(\max(a,b) < d < a+b\). Then
there is \(C=C(d,a,b)\) such that

\begin{equation*}{
f*g(x) \sim_{x\to \infty} C\Vert x\Vert^df(x)g(x).
}\end{equation*}

