[Lemma lem:determ_truncation of arXiv:2605.21265, 'The non-Hermitian minor process'] Assume the set-up and conditions of Theorem~(theo:main of the paper). For $k_j\in[N]$ denote $x_j:=k_j/N$, $j=1,2$, and assume that $x_1\le x_2$. For any $f_1,f_2\in H^{2+\delta}_0(\Omega)$ it holds that
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Cov} \left(L^{(k_1)}(f_1), L^{(k_2)}(f_2)\right) = \frac{1}{8\pi^2}\left(I_1+\bm{1}_{\beta=1}\widetilde{I}_1 +\kappa_4 x_1^2 I_2\right)+\mathcal{O}\left(N^{-c}\right),

\end{equation}
for some $N$-independent $c>0$. Here we denoted
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
&\int^\#: =   \int_\mathbf{C}\!\!\mathrm{d}^2 z_1\!\!\int_\mathbf{C}\!\!\mathrm{d}^2 z_2 \overline{\Delta f_1(z_1)}\Delta f_2(z_2)\int_0^{+\infty}\!\!\!\mathrm{d}\eta_1 \!\!\int_0^{+\infty}\mathrm{d}\eta_2,\\
I_1&: = \int^\#(-V_{12}), \qquad \widetilde{I}_1:= \int^\#(-V_{1\bar 2}),\qquad I_2:=\int^\# (-U_1U_2).
\end{split}
\end{equation}
The implicit constant in $\mathcal{O}(\cdot)$ in the rhs. of (equation eq:determ_truncation of the paper) is uniform in $x_j\in [c_0,1]$, $j=1,2$, and may depend on $\|\Delta f_j\|_{L^2(\Omega)}$ and $|\Omega|$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

