[Definition 7 of arXiv:2608.05842, 'Asymptotic Expansion of the Kallianpur–Striebel Formula under Perturbations of Linear Mode'] Let
\begin{align*}
  \eta_t^\epsilon = O_{\nu^\epsilon}^{T}(1)
\end{align*}
if a family of random variables $\{\eta_t^\epsilon\}_{0\leq \epsilon<1,t\geq 0}$ and family of probability measures $\{\nu_\epsilon\}_{0\leq \epsilon <1}$ on $\mathcal{F}$ satisfies
\begin{align*}
  \lim_{K\to \infty}\sup_{0\leq t\leq T}\sup_{0<\epsilon <r}\nu^\epsilon(|\eta_t^\epsilon|>K)=0
\end{align*}
for some $r>0$.
Furthermore, let us write $\eta^\epsilon=O_{\nu^\epsilon}^{T}(\epsilon^i)$ if
\begin{align*}
  \frac{\eta^\epsilon}{\epsilon^i}=O_{\nu^\epsilon}^{T}(1)
\end{align*}
for $i=0,1,2,\cdots$.

[Lemma lem:DMSboundA of arXiv:2608.29657, 'Hypocoercivity of Tempered Bouncy Particle Samplers for Heavy-Tailed Targets'] Let~(ass:wpi of the paper), (ass:sigmabounds of the paper) and~(ass:curvature of the paper) hold.
    For all $f \in C^1_c({\mathbb R}^d \times {\mathbb R}^d)$,
    \begin{equation}|\langle {\mathcal A} f, {\mathcal L} f \rangle_{L^2(\mu_\sigma )}| \leq \|f- \Pi f\|_{L^2(\mu_\sigma)}^2.\end{equation}

[Proposition 14 (Macroscopic mass) of arXiv:2608.04799, '2608.04799'] There is \(M=M(\lambda)<\infty\) such that
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{n\ge n_\lambda}n^{-2/3}
  \E\sum_{C:\,|C|\ge n^{2/3}}|C|\le M.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every \(B\ge1\),
\begin{equation}
  \sup_{n\ge n_\lambda}\Prob(X_{n,1}>B)\le M/B.
\end{equation}

