[Theorem finite time variance bound by asymptotic variance of arXiv:2606.01683, 'Singular-value gap of nonreversible Markov processes'] In the above setting, 
\begin{align} 
        \left|
        \operatorname{Var}_\mu(\mu_tg)
        -
        \frac{\sigma_g^2}{t}
        \right|
        \le
        \frac{4}{\gamma_K^2t^2}\|g\|^2 
\end{align}
for every \(g\in K\).
Consequently,
\begin{align} 
        \frac{\sigma_K^2}{t}
        -
        \frac{4}{\gamma_K^2t^2}
        \le
        \bigl(\Delta_t^K\bigr)^2
        \le
        \frac{\sigma_K^2}{t}
        +
        \frac{4}{\gamma_K^2t^2}.
\end{align}

