body:
[Theorem Thm-SES-IM of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Let (Hypo-SES H E of the paper) hold. Suppose there exists a deterministic initial state $x_0 \in \mathbf H$ such that the following conditions are met:
		\begin{enumerate}[label={\bf (\arabic*)},leftmargin=0.79cm]\setlength\itemsep{0.2em}
			\item The system (equation SES of the paper) admits a pathwise unique global solution $X(t,x_0)$ starting from $x_0$ which satisfies a uniform-in-time \textit{a priori} bound:
			\begin{equation}
				\sup_{t\ge0}\mathbb{E}\Big[f\big(\|X(t,x_0)\|_{\mathbf H}^2\big)\Big] < \infty,
			\end{equation}
			for some strictly increasing, continuous function $f:[0,\infty)\to [0,\infty)$ with $f(0)=0$ and $\lim_{r\to\infty} f(r)=\infty$.

			\item The Markov semigroup $\{\mathscr{P}_{t}\}_{t\ge0}$ defined by (equation Markov semigroup-SES of the paper) satisfies the restricted Feller property under mismatched metrics (cf. Definition (Locally Feller definition of the paper)) on the state space $E=\mathbf H$ equipped with  $\widetilde{d}_E=d_{\widetilde{\mathbf H}}$.
		\end{enumerate}
		Then there exists an invariant probability measure for $\{\mathscr{P}_{t}\}_{t\ge0}$ supported on $\mathbf H$ in the sense of Definition (IM definition of the paper).

