[Proposition prop:global_hajek of arXiv:2507.10531, 'Quantitative central limit theorems for exponential random graphs'] As in (equation eq:hatngdef of the paper), let us write
\begin{equation}
    \widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G(x) = \mathsf{N}_G(x) - 2 \mathsf{e} p^{\mathsf{e}-1} n^{\mathsf{v}-2} \mathsf{E}(x).
\end{equation}
Then, for all $\zeta \in (0,1)$, there is some $c > 0$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P}\mleft[\mleft|\widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G(X) - \mathbb{E}\mleft[\widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G(X)\mright]\mright| > n^{\mathsf{v}-1.5+\zeta}\mright] \leq \exp\mleft(-cn^\zeta\mright).
\end{equation}
In particular, for all $\xi > 0$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \operatorname{Var}\mleft[\widehat{\mathsf{N}}_G(X)\mright] \lesssim n^{2\mathsf{v}-3+\xi}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

