[Definition 2 (Regular right edge) of arXiv:2608.27307, '2608.27307'] We call $E_*\in\mb D_0$ a regular right edge of $\bnu$ if
        \begin{align}
                s_{\min}\left(AA^\top-(E_*+g(E_*))(I_M+m(E_*)\Sg)\right) & \geq\tau_0. 
        \end{align}
        $s_{\min}(\cdot)$ denotes the smallest singular value.
        A regular left edge is defined analogously, with the adjacent gap lying to the left of $E_*$.

[Proposition 24 (Cyclotomic-local knot germ) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] Fix a zero-framed knot $K$ and an integer $n\ge2$.  For every $d\ge1$
and $s\in\Z$, the series
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr J_{K,s}(z)=
 \sum_{k\ge0}b_k^{(n)}(K;q)U_k(z)
\end{equation}
converges in $\mathscr A_{d,s}$.  If $i\in\Z_{\ge0}$ and
$z_i\equiv z_s\pmod{\pi_d}$, then continuous evaluation at
$u_s=z_i-z_s$ gives
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr J_{K,s}(z_i)=J_i^{SU(n)}(K;q).
\end{equation}

[Theorem 9 of arXiv:2608.27500, 'Optimal Transport for Network Comparison: \\ A Review with Machine Learning Applications'] Let $G=(V,E)$ and $G'=(V,E')$ with $|V|=n$ be connected graphs. Then
    \begin{align*}
        \sum_{i=2}^n \bigg(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_i}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_i'}}\bigg)^2\leq BW(\mu,\nu)^2\leq \sum_{i=2}^n \bigg(\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_{n-i+2}}}-\frac{1}{\sqrt{\lambda_i'}}\bigg)^2.
    \end{align*}

