[Proposition 7 (Uniform two-convexity) of arXiv:2608.25971, 'Positive \texorpdfstring{$\tau$}{tau}-bi-Ricci curvature and Mean curvature flow with surg'] There is $\beta=\beta(n,\alpha_0)>0$ such that every hypersurface in
$\CC_{\tau,\kappa}(R,\alpha)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_1+\lambda_2\geq\beta H.
\end{equation}
One may take
\begin{equation}
 \beta=\frac{2\alpha_0}{2(n-2)+n\alpha_0}.
\end{equation}
Consequently,
\begin{equation*}
 -H\leq\lambda_1\leq\cdots\leq\lambda_n\leq H,
 \qquad \frac1nH^2\leq|A|^2\leq nH^2,
\end{equation*}
$\lambda_i\geq\beta H/2$ for $i\geq2$, and
\begin{equation}
 |H\nabla_i h_{kl}-(\nabla_iH)h_{kl}|^2
 \geq\frac{\beta^2}{8}H^2|\nabla H|^2.
\end{equation}

