[Prop 59 (Key estimate for the QVF) of arXiv:2510.22155, 'Random walks in space-time random media in all spatial dimensions: the full subcritical fl'] Let $\phi \in C_c^\infty(\mathbb R)$. Let $\z:I\to\mathbb R$ be the specific function from Definition \ref{z}. For all $t>0$,
		\begin{align}

			\lim_{N \to \infty}\;  \Ex\bigg[ \bigg( Q_N^{\z}(t,\phi)- \gamma(\z)\int_\mathbb R \int_0^t G(2s,x)^2 \phi(x)\dr x \dr s\bigg)^2 \bigg] = 0.
		\end{align}

[Lemma 13 of arXiv:2606.01881, '2606.01881'] There is a coupling of the first-table process with two Yule processes $Z^{(1)}$ and $Z^{(p)}$ such that
\begin{equation}
        N_1^{(n)}=Z^{(p)}(\tau_n),\qquad n\ge1.
\end{equation}

[Lemma lm:g406 of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] Consider a fixed   weight configuration $\omega\in\mathbb{R}^{\mathbb{Z}^2}$ and $k\in\mathbb{Z}$.  Suppose $\pi_{k:\infty}$ is a semi-infinite geodesic such that $\pi_n\cdote_i\to\infty$ for $i\in\{1,2\}$.   Then  for all $x\in\mathbb{Z}^2$ the  monotone nondecreasing  limit 
\begin{equation} 
 A(x,\pi_k) =  \lim_{n\to\infty}  ( L_{x,\pi_n} - L_{\pi_k, \pi_n} )    \end{equation}
exists in $(-\infty, \infty]$.  
On the  quadrant $\pi_k+\mathbb{Z}_+^2$ we have a finite  Busemann function 
\begin{equation}  
A(x,y) =  \lim_{n\to\infty}  ( L_{x,\pi_n} - L_{y, \pi_n} ) .    \end{equation}

