[Proposition 61 of arXiv:2609.03070, 'Variants of order semicontinuity in Banach lattices'] $F$ is $r$-$\sigma$-semicontinuous if and only if the common $\sigma$-order and $\mathrm{u\sigma o}$ closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is contained in $r\Ba_{F}$. Moreover, the following conditions are equivalent:
\item[(i)] $F$ is topologically $\sigma$-semicontinuous;
\item[(ii)] The norm topology is $\sigma$-semicontinuous;
\item[(iii)] The common $\sigma$-order and $\mathrm{u\sigma o}$ closure of $\Ba_{F}$ is norm bounded;
\item[(iv)] $\sigma$-order closure preserves norm bounded sets;
\item[(iv')] $\mathrm{u\sigma o}$ closure preserves norm bounded sets. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma L:MomentBounds of arXiv:2606.03079, 'Mean Field Limits for Stochastic, Underdamped Reactive Langevin Dynamics Models'] Let Assumptions (A:AssumptionRho of the paper) as well as Assumption (A:AssumptionMomentFinitenessGeneral of the paper) hold.
Then there exists a finite constant $C<\infty$ (not depending on $\zeta$) such that the following moment bound holds
\begin{align*}
\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\sum_{j=1}^{J} \theta^{\zeta,j,2p}_{t}&=\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\sum_{j=1}^{J}\mathbb{E}\left \langle |x|^{2p} +|v|^{2p},\mu^{\zeta,j}_{t}(dx,dv)\right\rangle \leq C<\infty,
\end{align*}
where the $p$ used above corresponds to the one from Assumption (A:AssumptionRho of the paper) and Assumption (A:AssumptionMomentFinitenessGeneral of the paper).

