[Lemma lemma measure Q of arXiv:2411.14350, 'Randomized Geodesic Flow on Hyperbolic Groups'] Recall the measure $\bar\mathbb{P}_g$ from Definition (def bi-inf RW of the paper). Then 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{Q} (A) := \sum_{g\in G} \bar\mathbb{P}_g(A \cap G_g^{\mathbb{Z}})
\end{equation}
is a well-defined measure on $G^{\mathbb{Z}}$, which is invariant under both the $\mathbb{Z}$-action and the $G$-action defined above.

