body:
[Prop 15 of arXiv:2604.12334, 'On additive averaging kernels for finite Markov chains'] For $P \in \mathcal{S}(\pi)$ and $G$ a Gibbs kernel defined on some partition $(\mathcal{O}_i)_{i=1}^k$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \KL{\widetilde{\pi}_\alpha}(Q_\alpha\ \|\ \widetilde{\Pi}_\alpha) = (1-\alpha)\KL{\pi} (G\| \Pi) + \alpha \KL{\pi}(P \| \Pi). 
    \end{equation}

[Proposition 2 (Information identity, ceiling, and comparison invariance) of arXiv:2609.02362, '\textbf{Farthest-cell triplet entropy: high-dimensional shell limits and hyperbolic curvat'] For every metric probability space,
\begin{equation}
  \log 3-\Htri(P,\metric)
  =I\{L_V(X);V\},

\end{equation}
and hence
\begin{equation}
  0\le \Htri(P,\metric)\le\log 3.
\end{equation}
Equality in the upper bound holds if and only if $q(V)=(1/3,1/3,1/3)$ almost surely. Moreover, the value is unchanged when every dissimilarity is transformed by a common strictly increasing function; in particular, it is invariant to global metric rescaling.

