[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2606.14876, 'High-Order Talagrand and Eldan--Gross Inequalities via Besov-Type Variance Functionals'] For all $k\in \Nbb_{\leq n}$, $f:\cube^n\to [-1,1]$, and $1\leq q\leq p\leq 2$,
\begin{equation}
    \frac{\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^p}^{p}}{\big[1+\frac{q}{2k(2-q)} \ln^{+}(\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^p}^{p}/\left\|\left|\grad^k f\right|\right\|_{\Leb^q}^{2})\big]^{kp/2}} \geq C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Lp-Lq-energy-Boolean}}}(p,q)^k \Wop^{\geq k}(f),
\end{equation}
with $C^{\text{\rm\ref{thm:high-order-Lp-Lq-energy-Boolean}}}(p,q) = \left(M(p)^{-\frac{2}{p}}+\frac{pq}{4\upe(2-q)}\right)^{-\frac{p}{2}}  \gtrsim 2-q$, where $M(p) := p \, 2^{-\frac{p}{2}} \max_{x\geq 0} \frac{1-\upe^{-x}}{x^{p/2}}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma lm:rem_bd of arXiv:2608.27828, 'Scaling limit of the 3D abelian Yang--Mills Langevin dynamics'] Under the same assumption as in lemma (lm:cubic_bd of the paper), one has
\begin{align}

& \sup_{t\in[0,T]} \|\varepsilon^{-2} \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}_\varepsilon^*\mathfrak{R}(\varepsilon^2 \mathop{}\!\mathrm{d}_\varepsilon (\Psi_i+v_i)(t)) \|_{\CC^{-1}_\varepsilon} \lesssim r^5\varepsilon^{\frac12-5\kappa}.
\end{align}

