[Corollary main global corollary of arXiv:2606.01683, 'Singular-value gap of nonreversible Markov processes'] Assume the global singular-value gap $\gamma$ defined in (equation gap definition continuous time of the paper) 
    satisfies $\gamma > 0$. Then 
    \begin{align*}


        &\text{(i)} \qquad \Delta_t \leq \frac{2}{\sqrt{\gamma \mkern1mu t}} \\
        &\text{(ii)} \sup_{s \in [t, 2t]}  \Delta_s \geq \frac{1}{\frac{3}{2} \gamma \mkern1mu t  + 3}
    \end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem th_hydrodynamics of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] {(Hydrodynamic Limit)}
Let $\gamma: [0,1] \rightarrow [0,1]$  {be a measurable function and $(\nu_N)_{N \geq 1}$ a }sequence of probability measures on $\Omega_N$ which are associated to the initial profile $\gamma$. Then,  {for every $G \in C([0,1])$, every $t \in [0,T]$ and every $\delta > 0$,}
\begin{equation}
 \lim _{N\to\infty } \mathbb P_{\nu_{N}}\Big(\;\Big| \langle \pi^N_t,G\rangle - \int_0^1 G(x) \rho_t(x) dx\Big| > \delta \Big)= 0,
\end{equation}
where  $\rho_{t}(\cdot)$ is the unique weak solution of (equation PDEproblem of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 9 (The $m$th-order Santal\'o inequality on $\R^n$) of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Fix $Q\in\conbodo[m].$ Let $K\subset \R^n$ be a compact set of positive volume such that $K$ or $K^\circ$ has center of mass at the origin. Then,
  \begin{equation}
  \Vol(K^{\star,Q})\vol(K)^m \leq \vol(\B)^m \Vol((B_2^n)^{\star,Q}).

\end{equation}
There is equality if and only if $K=E$ for some centered ellipsoid $E\subset\R^n$ up to removal of null sets. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary prop:cooling-scgf of arXiv:2603.22652, 'A cohesive account on the ergodic behaviours and scaling limits of Random Walks in Cooling'] {Consider a cooling map $\tau$ as in (equation effective-cooling of the paper) and an environment law $\mu$ as in (equation eq:mu_iid of the paper). Let $X = (X_n, n \in {\mathbb {Z}}_+)$ be the annealed RWCRE obtained from $P^{ \mu, \tau}_0$ as defined in (equation eq:annealed_rwcre of the paper),} and for each $\theta \in {\mathbb {R}}$ let $I^*(\theta): = \lim_{T \to \infty} \frac{1}{T} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta Z_T}]$, where $Z = (Z_n, n \in {\mathbb {Z}}_+)$ is the RWRE obtained from $P^\mu$ as defined in (equation eq:annealed_rwre of the paper). Then  
    \begin{equation}
    \begin{aligned}
        \lim_n \frac{1}{n} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta X_n}]&= \lim_n \sum_k \frac{T_{k,n}}{n} \frac{1}{T_{k,n}} \log {\mathbb {E}}[e^{\theta Z_{T_{k,n}}}] = I^*(\theta).
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
{In particular, under the annealed measures, the empirical speeds of RWRE and RWCRE satisfy the same rate $n$ LDP with rate function given by the Legendre-Fenchel transform of $I^*$.}

