[Cor of arXiv:2411.14090, '{\bf Exponential Ergodicity in $\W_1$ for SDEs with Distribution Dependent Noise and Parti'] Assume that (i), (ii) and (equation monotonicity of the paper) in {\bf(A1)} hold for $$\phi(v)=\left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
l_1v, & \hbox{$v\leq r_0$,}\\
    \left\{-\frac{l_1+l_2}{r_0}(v-r_0)+l_1\right\}v, &\hbox{$r_0< v\leq 2r_0$,}\\
    -l_2v, & \hbox{$r>2r_0$}
  \end{array}
\right.
$$
with some positive constants $l_1, l_2, r_0.$ Then (iii) in {\bf(A1)} holds and consequently, the assertions in Theorem (main thm of the paper) hold.

[Lemma lem:731 of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] For all $1\le i\le n$, $1\le j\le m$, $n>n_2$, and $z\inT_{i,j}$, we have\begin{equation}
        \mathbb{P}_{z}\Big(\tau_{\widetildeT_{i, j}}\ge\tau_{\partial \widetilde{B}(z)}\Big)\ge\frac{1}{2}.
    \end{equation}

