[Theorem thm:NA1_NA2_converse of arXiv:2609.00794, 'On operators whose adjoints or second adjoints attain their norms'] Let $Y$ be a non-reflexive Banach space. Then 
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
        \itemsep0.25em
        \item $\operatorname{QNA}(\ell_1,Y)\neq \operatorname{NA}_1 (\ell_1,Y)$; 
        \item If, in addition, $Y$ contains no isomorphic copy of $\ell_1$, then $\operatorname{NA}_1(\ell_1, Y) \not= \operatorname{NA}_2(\ell_1, Y)$.
    \end{enumerate}

