[Lem typT 1 suc of arXiv:2608.25471, 'Exact Hausdorff measures and fine geometry of collisions of independent Markov processes'] Let $a_1$ be the constant in Lemma~(lem:typT poly LB of the paper)
  and fix a compact set $K\subseteq M$.
  Define $H^{\mathrm{t}}_{n,K} \coloneqq \bigcap_{j=0}^{N_n-1}\{\hat{X}_{t_j(n)}\in K^k\}$.
  Then there exists a constant $c_K \in (0,\infty)$ such that, for all sufficiently large $n\in\mathbb{N}$,
  \begin{equation}
    \sup_{x\in M}
    \hat{P}_{\diag(x)}\!\left(
      H^{\mathrm{t}}_{n,K}
      \cap
      \bigcap_{j=0}^{N_n-1}
      \left\{
        C_{\delta_{\ell_{j+1}(n)}}\!\circ\hat{\theta}_{t_j(n)}
        <a_1\Psi_{\mathrm{ct}}(\delta_{\ell_{j+1}(n)})
      \right\}
    \right)
    \leq
    \frac{c_K}{n\log n}.
  \end{equation}

