\begin{equation*}
B : = \{y^* \otimes x^{**}\colon y^* \in S_{Y^*}, x^{**} \in S_{X^{**}}\}
\end{equation*}
is a James boundary for $\mathcal{L}_{w^*, w^*}(Y^*, X^*)$. 

Notice that, on $\mathcal{L}_{w^*, w^*}(Y^*, X^*)$, the topology $\sigma(\mathcal{L}_{w^*, w^*}(Y^*, X^*), B)$ coincides with the WOT topology. Suppose, for contradiction, that there exists $K \subseteq \mathcal{L}_{w^*, w^*}(Y^*, X^*)$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
0 \in \overline{K}^{\operatorname{WOT}} \ \ \ \mbox{and} \ \ \ 0 \not\in \overline{\co}^{\|\cdot\|}(K).
\end{equation*}
