[Lemma lem:uniqueness of arXiv:2608.18293, 'Critical tensor covariance at the Marchenko--Pastur threshold'] Let $\nu$ be any probability measure on $[0,\infty)$, $c>0$, and $z\in\mathbb{C}_+$. The equation
\begin{equation}
  \frac1m+z
  =\int_0^\infty\frac{r}{1+crm}\,\nu(\,\mathrm{d} r)

\end{equation}
has at most one solution $m\in\mathbb{C}_+$.

