[Theorem 3 ({\cite[(1.16)) of arXiv:2608.18834, 'The Parabolic Anderson Model's Total Mass at Small Times: Geometry, Fluctuations, and Reno'] {BurchardSchmuckenschlager}}]

For every bounded domain $D$,
\begin{align}

|D|-\int_D u_0(t,x)\d x\gtrsim t^{1/2}.
\end{align}
In other words, the total mass cannot converge to $|D|$ at a faster rate than $t^{1/2}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem 1 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] Let $\Omega$ be a bounded open subset of $\R^d$ with $C^{1,1}$ boundary, and $X=(X_t)_{t\ge 0}$ be a translation invariant isotropic stochastic process satisfying Assumption~\ref{assump1}. Then,
		\begin{align}
			\lim_{t\downarrow 0}\frac{\Vol(\Omega)-Q^X_\Omega(t)}{\mu(t)}=\Per(\Omega),
		\end{align}
		where $\Per(\Omega)$ denotes the perimeter of $\Omega$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 12 (Local $C^0$ estimate) of arXiv:2608.29736, '2608.29736'] There exists a constant \(C>0\), independent of \(t\), such that
\begin{equation}
u_t\geq\rho-C\qquad\text{on }M\setminus Z.
\end{equation}
Consequently, for every \(K\Subset M\setminus Z\), there exists
\(C_K>0\), independent of \(t\), such that
\begin{equation}
-C_K\leq u_t\leq0\qquad\text{on }K.
\end{equation}

[Cor 158 of arXiv:2608.29416, 'Algorithmic threshold for high-dimensional projection pursuit I: general theory'] For all $\ell\leq \ubl$, we have 
  \begin{equation}

  \lim_{\eta\downarrow 0}
  \bbE\big[
  \hat{b}^{\chaos,\ell}(\hat X^{\ell,\eta})
  \big]
  =
  \lim_{\eta\downarrow 0}
  \bbE\big[
  \hat{b}^{\chaos,\ell}(\hat{\prxX}^{\ell,\eta}) \big]
  =
  0\,.
  \end{equation}

[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2512.02922, 'Asymptotics for additive functionals of particle systems via Stein's method'] For the model described in Section~\ref{eq:fractionalbrownianmotionparticles}, when $\mathbf{X}^{i,x}$ is a fractional Brownian motion and $Hd<1$, there exists a constant $c>0$ such that 
\[
\sigma_r^2 \;\geq\; c\, r^{2(1-H)}\Big[
     r^{\frac{3}{2}H}\Indi{\{d=1\}}
   + r^H\log(r)\Indi{\{d=2\}}
   + r^H\Indi{\{d\geq 3\}}
\Big].
\]

