[Cor 3.5 of arXiv:2603.13873, '{Solvability of BSDEs with possibly unbounded stochastic coefficients \\ on a general weig'] Let $\xi\in L_\tau^p(0;{\mathbb R}^k)$ and the generator $g$ satisfy assumptions (A:H1b of the paper) and (A:H2 of the paper)-(A:H5 of the paper). Assume further that for any $\bar p>1$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{E}\left[\exp\left(\bar p \int_0^\tau\left(\mu_t+\frac{\theta}{2[1\wedge(p-1)]}\nu_t^2\right)^+ {\rm d}t\right)\right]<+\infty.
\end{align}
Then, BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) admits a unique solution $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}\in \cap_{q\in(1,p)}H_\tau^q(0;{\mathbb R}^{k}\times{\mathbb R}^{k\times d})$.\vspace{0.1cm}

