body:
[Theorem 4 of arXiv:2604.01978, 'Homogenized Transformers'] Fix $d, n\ge 2$ and $\upbeta\in[0,1]$, and assume that $\langle x_i(0),x_j(0)\rangle\ge \gamma$ for $i\neq j$ and $\gamma\in(0, 1)$. Define the empirical mean
\begin{equation*} 
m(t)\coloneqq\frac{1}{n^2}\sum_{i=1}^n\sum_{j=1}^n \langle x_i(t),x_j(t)\rangle.
\end{equation*}
Let $u$ be the unique solution to the  Cauchy problem for the logistic equation
\begin{equation} 
\begin{cases}
\dot{u}(t)=u(t)(1-u(t)) \\
u(0)=m(0).
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
Then there exists a universal constant $C>0$ such that for every every $T>0$ and every $\delta\in(0,1)$, with probability at least $1-\delta$, the solution to \eqref{eq:Diffusive_gaussian_case} satisfies
\begin{equation}
\sup_{t\in[0,T]}\left|m(t)-u(t)\right|
\le Ce^{CT}\max\left(\frac{1}{d},\,d^{2}\sigma_{\bA}^{4}\upbeta^{2}\right)
+ C\sqrt{\frac{T}{d}\log\left(\frac{4}{\delta}\right)}.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Cor 7. cor: GW tree satisfies the sub-aging assumption of arXiv:2412.08236, 'Aging and sub-aging for Bouchaud trap models on resistance metric spaces'] Define a probability measure $\tilde{p} = (\tilde{p}_{k})_{k \geq 1}$ on $\mathbb{N}$ 
  by setting $\tilde{p}_{k} \coloneqq p_{k-1}$.
  Then, it holds that 
  \begin{equation}
    (T_{n}^{GW}, n^{-1/2}d_{T_{n}^{GW}}, \rho_{T_{n}^{GW}}, n^{-1} \dot{\mu}^{\#}_{T_{n}^{GW}})
    \xrightarrow{\mathrm{d}}
    (T_{2e}, d_{2e}, \rho_{2e}, \mu_{2e} \otimes \tilde{p})
  \end{equation}
  in the space $\mathfrak{M}_{c}(\markedfinMeasFunct{\mathbb{R}_{\geq 0}})$.

