Since the sequence $(\tau_n)_{n \geq 0}$ of stopping times is non-decreasing, it has a possibly infinite limit  $\tau$. As $X_{n+1}(t)=X_n(t)$ for all ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:27197ebd5f0b83551e2138e862ecc3e9f4a654177653c32f9a70a3247033e75e","revision_digest":"sha256:df0f2b64f2670e176de0f45b185a54332e1fef487a3eee967680eb4c05b117ba","source_id":"arxiv:2605.13727","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

