[Cor 3.1 of arXiv:2608.00420, '{Weighted $L^p$ solutions of scalar BSDEs with general unbounded stochastic coefficients}\'] Let the generator $g$ satisfy assumption (A:H1 of the paper) plus $\mu_\cdot\in {\mathbb R}_+$ (or assumption (A:H1 of the paper)(i)-(ii) plus (equation eq:2.3* of the paper) or assumption (A:H1' of the paper)) with the nonnegative process $f_\cdot$ satisfying $\mathbb{E}\left[(\int_0^\tau f_t{\rm d}t)^{p}\right]<+\infty$ instead of (equation eq:2.2 of the paper). Assume further that for some constant $M>0$,
\begin{align}
\int_0^\tau\left(\mu_t+\frac{\theta}{2(p-1)}\nu_t^2\right)^+{\rm d}t\leq M.
\end{align}
Then, for each $\xi\in L_\tau^p(0;{\mathbb R})$, BSDE (equation BSDE1.1 of the paper) admits an adapted solution $(y_t,z_t)_{t\in[0,\tau]}$ such that $y_\cdot\in S_\tau^p(0;{\mathbb R})$. Furthermore, if
\begin{align}
\int_0^\tau\left(\mu_t+\frac{\theta}{2[1\wedge(p-1)]}\nu_t^2\right)^+{\rm d}t\leq M,
\end{align}
then $z_\cdot\in M_\tau^p(0;{\mathbb R}^{d})$.

