[Lemma l.semi of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] The function $\Phi: \mathbb{RP}^1\times Y\times \mathcal{K}^{n_0}\to \mathbb{R}\cup \{\infty\}$ defined by
  $$
\Phi(v, p, \mu_1, \mu_2, \ldots, \mu_{n_0})=\left\{
  \begin{array}{ll}
    \infty, & \hbox{if $\chi(\{0\})>0$;} \\
    \mathop{\rm Var}\nolimits \log\left|p\circ(B_{\mu_{n_0}}\ldots B_{\mu_1})v\right|, & \hbox{if $\chi(\{0\})=0$,}
  \end{array}
\right.
$$
is lower semicontinuous.

