body:
[Lemma convergence of s-periods of arXiv:2609.02073, 'Existence of closed non-planar $p$-elasticae'] Let $(\lambda_n,C^2_n) \to (\lambda, C^2) \in S^0 \cup \partial S_{1}^0$ such that $(\lambda,C^2) \neq (\frac{p-1}{2},0)$ and $\lambda<p-1$. 
  Moreover, let $g_n:=g_{\lambda_n,C^2_n}$ and $g:=g_{\lambda,C^2}$. Then 
  \begin{equation*}
    S_n: [0,1] \to \R: w\mapsto \begin{cases}
      \int_{w_{m,n}}^w \frac{1}{\sqrt{g_n(x)}}dx &\text{if }w_{m,n}<w\leq1, \\ 0  &\text{if }0\leq w\leq w_{m,n},
    \end{cases}
  \end{equation*}
  converges pointwise to 
  \begin{equation*}
    S:[0,1] \to \R: w \mapsto \begin{cases}
      \int_{w_{m}}^w \frac{1}{\sqrt{g(x)}}dx &\text{if }w_{m}<w\leq 1, \\ 0  &\text{if }0\leq w\leq w_{m},
    \end{cases}
  \end{equation*}
  for any $w \in [0,1]$.

