body:
[Theorem thm:Qeq of arXiv:2608.16915, 'Exact mean--covariance dynamics of the Weber field in the stochastic Lagrangian representa'] The tensor $Q$ solves
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal D_uQ+G^\top Q+QG=2\nu\sum_{k=1}^3(\partial_kM)^\top(\partial_kM),\qquad Q(0)=0,
\end{equation}
and, with $S:=\tfrac12(G+G^\top)$ the symmetric strain,
\begin{equation}
  \mathcal D_u\tr Q+2\tr(SQ)=2\nu\left\lvert \nabla M\right\rvert_{\mathrm F}^2.
\end{equation}

[Definition def:APZ of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] A line ensemble $\mathbf{X}$ is asymptotically pinned to zero if for any $ \varepsilon, T > 0$ there is some
$k \in \mathbb{N}$ such that
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[ \sup_{t \in [-T,T]} X^k(t) \leqslant \varepsilon \mright] \geqslant 1 - \varepsilon.
\end{equation}

[Define of arXiv:2601.09990, 'Remarks on the convex integration technique applied to singular stochastic partial differe'] \rm{(\hspace{1sp}[H14])} Let $\alpha < 0$ and $r = - \lceil \alpha \rceil > 0$. We say $\xi \in \mathcal{S}'$ belongs to $\mathscr{C}_{\mathfrak{s}}^{\alpha}$ if it belongs to the dual of $C_{c}^{r}(\mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{T}^{d})$ and for every compact set $K \subset \mathbb{R} \times \mathbb{T}^{d}$ there exists a constant $C$ such that 
\begin{align*}
\langle \xi, \mathscr{S}_{\mathfrak{s},\bar{z}}^{\delta} \eta \rangle  \leq C \delta^{\alpha} \hspace{3mm} \forall \, \eta \in \{ \psi \in C^{r}: \lVert \psi \rVert_{C^{r}} \leq 1, \supp \psi \subset B_{\mathfrak{s}}(0,1)\},  
\end{align*}
for all $\delta \in (0, 1]$ and all $\bar{z} \in K$.

[Lemma lem:two-slab of arXiv:2607.06249, 'Extreme least singular values of Gaussian row submatrices and a phase retrieval stability '] For each $\mathbb{F}\in\{\mathbb{R},\mathbb{C}\}$ there is a constant $C_\mathbb{F}$ such that, for $0<t\le1$,
\begin{equation}
  q_D^\mathbb{F}(t)\le (1+C_\mathbb{F} t^2)p_\mathbb{F}(t)^2\left(1+\frac{C_\mathbb{F}}{D}\right),\qquad D\ge3,
\end{equation}
and $q_2^\mathbb{F}(t)\le p_\mathbb{F}(t)$.

