[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2506.18558, '2506.18558'] Suppose that Assumptions {\rm\ref{A1}}, {\rm\ref{A2}} and {\rm\ref{A3}} hold.  Let  $\{\mu^x_{t}\}_{t\in\RR}$ be an evolution system of measures  given in Lemma $\ref{Le3.3}$, and $\mu^x$ be the invariant probability measure given above. Then,
\begin{align}
\mathbb{W}_1(\mu^x_t, \mu^x)\le C(1+|x|)\left[e^{-\beta t}+\int^t_0 e^{-\beta (t-u)}\phi_2(u)\,du\right],   
\end{align}
where $\beta>0$ is defined in Lemma $\ref{L3.1}$.

