[Lemma 9 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(\beta\in(0,1/6)\). There are \(n_0,\lambda_0, r_0\geq 0\) and \(c>0\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), any \(\lambda_0\leq \lambda\leq n^{\beta}\), any \(1\leq k\leq n\), and any \(L\geq r_0 \sqrt{\lambda}n^{2/3}\) with \(k+L\leq n\),
    \begin{equation*}
        P\bigl( \bar{A}^{\lambda}_{k,k+L} \bgiven (A^{\lambda}_{k-L,k-1})^c, (A^{\lambda}_{k+L+1,k+2L})^c\bigr)
        \leq
        \exp(-c\tfrac{\lambda L}{n^{2/3}}).
    \end{equation*}

