[Definition 5 of arXiv:2609.01098, 'Gaussian upper bounds for averaged heat semigroups on graphs'] The {\em relative Faber-Krahn inequality} $FK_a(n,r_1,r_2)$ holds in $B$, if for all $x\in B$, $r\in[r_1,r_2]$ and $U\subset B_x(r) $, we have
\begin{equation*}
\lambda(U):=\inf_{u\in\cC_c(U),\|u\|_2= 1}\cE(u)\geq \frac{a}{r^2}\left(\frac{m(B_x(r))}{m(U)}\right)^\frac{2}{n}.
\end{equation*}

