[Lemma lem:odometer-derivative of arXiv:2609.02829, 'Quantitative explosion and percolation of the divisible sandpile'] Suppose $(\zeta(x))_{x\in\mathbb{Z}^d}$ are independent and atomless. Then,
	$\mathbb{P}$-almost surely, for every $n\geq1$ and $x,z\in\mathbb{Z}^d$,
	\begin{equation}
		\partial_{\zeta(z)}u_n(x)
		=
		\mathbf E_x\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}
		\mathbf{1}_{\{X_j=z\}}
		\prod_{i=0}^j\mathbf{1}_{\{u_{n-i}(X_i)>0\}}
		=
		\mathbf E_x\sum_{j=0}^{n-1}
		\mathbf{1}_{\{X_j=z\}}\mathbf{1}_{\{\tau_n^*>j\}}\, .
	\end{equation}

