[Definition 9 of arXiv:2608.29984, 'On Cauchy Problems for Parabolic Equations with Rough Coefficients'] Given $f\in L^{1}_{loc}(\R^{d})$, we say $f\in BMO(\R^{d})$ provided
\begin{equation}
[f]_{BMO}:=\sup_{Q}\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q}|f-(f)_{Q}|dx,\ (f)_{Q}=\frac{1}{|Q|}\int_{Q}f(y)dy,
\end{equation}
the supermum is taken in all cubes in $\R^{d}$.

