body:
[Lemma lem:mgf of arXiv:2411.16366, 'Connections between sequential Bayesian inference and evolutionary dynamics'] \textbf{Moment generating function}.  Consider 
\begin{align*}
Y_t = \int_0^t \vartheta_s dW_s 
\end{align*}
where $\vartheta_s$ is a deterministic, scalar-valued continuous function of $s$ and $W_t$ is a real-valued Brownian motion wrt a probability measure $\mathbb{P}$.  Then 
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}^\mathbb{P}[\exp(\lambda Y_t)] = \exp \left( \frac{\lambda}{2} \int_0^t \vartheta_s^2 ds \right) 
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

