[Lemma Lemma-Q2 n m of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] Suppose that $0\le \theta<s-3\delta_2$, where $\delta_2=\delta_{\mathcal Q_2}$ is given in (equation delta-Qi of the paper).  Let (Hypo-W L of the paper) hold and let $\wp_n$ be the Marcus flow 
		given by (equation regular Marcus flow Q2 of the paper). Then there is a function $\lambda_{\cdot,\cdot}:\mathbb N\times\mathbb N\to(0,1)$ with $\displaystyle \lim_{n,m\to\infty} 
		\lambda_{n,m}=0$ such that  for all $f,g\in H_d^s$ and $r\in[0,1]$,
		\begin{align}
			\left|\|\wp_n\big(r,l,f\big)-\wp_m\big(r,l,g\big)\|^2_{H^{\theta}}-\|f-g\|^2_{H^{\theta}}\right| \lesssim |l|\Big(\lambda_{n,m}(\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{H^{s}}+\left\lVertg\right\rVert_{H^{s}})^2+\|f-g\|^2_{H^{\theta}}\Big),
		\end{align} 
		\begin{align}
			\Big|\|\wp_n\big(r,l,f\big)-\wp_m\big(r,l,g\big)\|^2_{H^{\theta}} - \|f-g\|^2_{H^{\theta}}  &-  2l\cdot\bIP{\mathcal Q_{2,n} f-\mathcal Q_{2,m} g ,f-g}_{H^\theta}\Big|\notag\\
			& \lesssim  |l|^2\Big(\lambda_{n,m}(\left\lVertf\right\rVert_{H^{s}}+\left\lVertg\right\rVert_{H^{s}})^2+\|f-g\|^2_{H^{\theta}}\Big).
		\end{align}

