body:
[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2512.02661, 'Worst-case mixing estimates for Brownian motion with semipermeable barriers'] There exist absolute constants $\delta_0,c>0$ such that the following holds for $\delta \leq \delta_0$.
	For every $x_0\in D$, measurable $E\subseteq D$, and $t \geq c\min\{ 1/\kappa^2, 1/\lambda_{\max}^2,\rho^2 \}$,
	\begin{equation}
		\bbP\bigl(X_t \in E \mid X_0 = x_0\bigr)
		\geq
		\frac{1}{2}
		\sup_{u}\inf_{x_0' \in \cD(\delta)}\bbP\bigl(X_{u} \in E \mid X_0 = x_0'\bigr)
		.

	\end{equation}
	Here, the supremum runs over $u \leq  t - c\min\{ 1/\kappa^2, 1/\lambda_{\max}^2,\rho^2\}$.

