[Proposition 10 (Reduction to records) of arXiv:2608.16752, 'Absorption Probabilities for Random Convex Hulls: Distribution-Freeness via the Wall-Cross'] Let $u_1, \dots, u_n$ be unit vectors in $\R^d$ in general linear
    position, and for $R > 1$ set
    \begin{align*}
        \lambda_R := \big(u_1 \, |\, R\,u_2 \, |\,  R^2 u_3\, | \,  \dots \, | \,
        R^{n-1} u_n\big) \in \R^{d\times n}.
    \end{align*}
    Then there is $R_0 = R_0(u_1, \dots, u_n)$ such that for every
    $R \ge R_0$ the configuration $\lambda_R$ is regular and, for every
    $g = (\sigma, \varepsilon) \in \mathfrak{B}_n$,
    \begin{equation}
        0 \in H(g\lambda_R)
        \iff
        0 \in \Conv\big( \varepsilon_i\, u_{\sigma(i)} \;:\;
           i\in \mathrm{Rec}(\sigma) \big).
    \end{equation}

