{"artifact_digest":"sha256:58faffbb15381716c462ace6a0b444612babc303338cba1df1563efec5411688","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/58/58faffbb15381716c462ace6a0b444612babc303338cba1df1563efec5411688.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:b1d56a56dde68ea21de25f1b729510be09200947018c2fcd8a9b7785b3f95347","bundle_entry_key":"bernoulli-cluster-thinning-threshold-bound","bundle_id":"population.critical-percolation-thinning-bridge-001","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"w441/bundle_001.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:probability.percolation.critical:bernoulli-cluster-thinning-threshold-bound","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Let G be any countable graph and let p_c(G)=inf{r:P_r(some infinite open cluster exists)>0}. Take a Bernoulli-p edge configuration omega, p>0. For almost every omega, every infinite component C of the open-edge graph has its own Bernoulli bond threshold p_c(C)>=min{1,p_c(G)/p}. In particular, any putative infinite critical cluster has p_c(C)=1.

Proof: for each rational q in (0,1) with pq<p_c(G), take a fresh family eta of independent Bernoulli-q bits, independent of all omega bits. The products omega_e eta_e are mutually independent Bernoulli-pq bits. They have no infinite component almost surely. By Tonelli, their conditional probability of an infinite component given omega is zero for almost every omega. On the open edges of each C, eta is precisely independent bond percolation on C. For this fixed rational q there are at most countably many components, so all have zero q-percolation probability. Intersect the probability-one sets for countably many rational q. Monotonicity then gives the threshold bound for every component, including parameters arbitrarily close to min{1,p_c(G)/p}. At p=p_c>0 the bound is one. On a bounded-degree infinite graph p_c>0 by the self-avoiding-path union bound. A connected locally finite quasi-transitive graph has bounded degree and is countable, so this applies to the target.

This is an elementary deduction, with no novelty claim and no independent review yet. Conditional independence is used only after introducing fresh eta; selected clusters are not declared independent of omega.","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:01f5472ebb869472b5d75049ecf42557b199c6165f836a799d663090e3d82d59","revision_digest":"sha256:eea2dc19fd5aa626c250d29fddf8149fcaee24722922657006c6d9a33c48bc7c","source_id":"owner:w441:P0043:2026-10-10:bernoulli-cluster-thinning-threshold-bound","source_revision":"draft-as-written-2026-10-10","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

