{"artifact_digest":"sha256:751f80288270a6100e178f0d2d6d6147a3bda1b92a42f8cecad21fc4be303a80","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/75/751f80288270a6100e178f0d2d6d6147a3bda1b92a42f8cecad21fc4be303a80.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:8ad37070b3cd0df112a7c2f0b45cdf5d1aed8d65b183605030d79225ca1e5619","bundle_entry_key":"2606-02036-theorem-11-determinant","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_043","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_043.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-02036-theorem-11-determinant","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: The fact that there exists a modification of the solution to \eqref{eq:Eq_interaction} that is a stochastic flow of diffeomorphisms follows from \cite{dorogovtsev2023measure}. 
The Jacobian matrix $\D x(v,t),\ v\in\mbR^d,\ t\geqslant 0$ satisfies the following stochastic differential equation 
\begin{align}

\begin{cases}
\differential{\D x}(v,t)=\D a(x(v,t),\mu_t)\D x(v,t)\differential{t}+\int_{\mbR^d}\D b(x(v,t),\mu_t,z)W(\differential{t},\differential{z})\D x(v,t),\\	
\D x(v,0)=I_{d},\ v\in\mbR^d,\\
\mu_t=\mu_0\circ x(\cdot,t)^{-1},\ t\geqslant 0,
