body:
[Question question-main-3 of arXiv:2604.04882, 'On a Problem of M. Kac on Laplace Distributions'] Let $D\subset\C$ and let $\Phi:D\times D\to\C$ be a map such that for every pair of characteristic functions $f_1,f_2$ on $\R$, the quantity $\Phi(f_1(\xi),f_2(\xi))$ is well defined for every $\xi\in\R$. Let $\cM$ be a subfamily of the set of all characteristic functions on $\R$. Suppose that
    \begin{align}
        \Phi(f_1(\xi),f_2(\xi))\in \cM
        \qquad\text{for all }\xi\in\R.
    \end{align}
    Under what conditions can one conclude that $f_1,f_2\in \cM$? (Stated as a question by the paper; open unless the paper says otherwise.)

[Definition def:thd of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] A bounded domain $D$ is called a twisted H\"older domain of order $\alpha$, $\alpha\in (0,1]$, if there exist positive constants $C_1,\ldots,C_5$, a point $x_0\in D$ and a bounded continuous function $\delta:D\to(0,\infty)$ such that the following properties (i), (ii) and (iii) hold.

(i) $\delta(x)\le C_1\,\mathrm{dist}(x,\partial D)^\alpha$ for all $x\in D$;

(ii) For all $x\in D$, there exists a rectifiable curve $\gamma_x\subseteq D$ connecting $x$ and $x_0$ such that $$\delta(x')\ge C_2\big(\delta(x)+l(\gamma_x(x,x'))\big)$$ for all $x'$ lying on $\gamma_x$, where $l(\gamma_x(x,x'))$ denotes the length of the piece of curve connecting $x$ and $x'$;

(iii) Let $F_a:=\{y\in D:\delta(y)\le a\}$. For any $a\le C_5$ and $x\in F_a$,
\begin{equation}
\mathrm{Cap}(B(x,C_3a)\cap F_a^c)\geq C_4\mathrm{Cap}(B(x,C_3a)),
\end{equation}
where $\mathrm{Cap}(\cdot)$ is the Newtonian capacity in $\mathbb{R}^3$ (see Definition 4.31 in [BM1]).

[Lemma 16 of arXiv:2606.31596, 'The Invariant Measure of Multiscale Markov Chains via Fast Arborescence Factorization'] Let $\tau\in \mathcal T$. Let $M\in \mathcal M$ be a minimal class. If at least one of the following properties is verified then $\tau\not\in \mathcal T^F$: 
\begin{itemize}	
\item[i)] $\tau$ is rooted at $x\in M$ 
and contains an edge going out from $M$;
\item[ii)] 
$\tau$ contains two or more edges going out from $M$;
\item[iii)] 
$\tau$ contains a slow edge connecting two points of $M$.
\end{itemize}

[Lem 32 of arXiv:2608.28148, 'Flows and homotopies of Banach Lie algebroids'] For a local section $\mathfrak{v}$ of $A_U$ we use the notation from \Cref{setup:PF_PB}. 
Then, for every $x \in U$ for which the expressions are defined, 
\begin{align}
\left. \frac{\partial}{\partial t} \right|_{t=s} (\mathfrak{F}^{t,s}_\mathfrak{u})^*\mathfrak{v}(x) = \LB[\mathfrak{u}_s,\mathfrak{v}]_A(x). 
\end{align}

[Lemma 11 of arXiv:2606.30349, 'Attenuated Poisson Dirichlet approximations for divisibility configurations'] There exists a constant \(C>0\) such that, for all \(n\) sufficiently large,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal E_{A^o}[\mathcal X_n^{\mathrm{geo}},\mathcal X_n^0]
\le
C\frac{\log\log n}{\log n}.
\end{align*}
In particular,
\begin{align*}
\mathcal E_{A^o}[\mathcal X_n^{\mathrm{geo}},\mathcal X_n^0]
\le
C\frac{(\log\log n)^{\mathrm e-\frac32}}{\log n}.
\end{align*}

