[Lemma 15 of arXiv:2511.09280, 'Random Walk conditioned to stay above a non-flat floor: curvature effects'] Let \(\beta>0, p\geq 1\). Then, there are \(c>0, n_0\geq 1, \lambda_0\geq 1\) such that for any \(n\geq n_0\), \(\lambda \geq \lambda_0\) with \(\lambda n^{\alpha_p}< n/2^p\),
    \begin{equation*}
        \mu_n^{0,h_n^+}(\varphi_0\geq \lambda n^{\alpha_p}+n)
        \leq
        e^{-c\lambda^{(2p-1)/p}}.
    \end{equation*}

