[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2506.09592, 'Extremal process of the local time of simple\\random walk on a regular tree'] For each~$t>0$, the weak limit \eqref{E:1.18} exists and defines an a.s.-finite random Borel measure~$Z_t$ on~$[0,1]$. Moreover, there exists a Borel probability measure~$\nu$ on~$\R^\N$ such that for all~$t>0$, all~$f\in\Cloc^+$ and all sequences $\{k_n\}_{n\in\N}$ with $k_n\to\infty$ and $n-k_n\to\infty$, 
\begin{equation}

\begin{aligned}
E^\varrho\bigl(&\texte^{-\langle\zeta_{n,k_n}^{(t)},f\rangle}\bigr)
\\
&\,\,\,\underset{n\to\infty}\longrightarrow\,\, \E\biggl(\exp\Bigl\{-\int Z_t(\textd x)\otimes\texte^{-2\slb\, h}\textd h\otimes\nu(\textd\phi)(1-\texte^{-f(x,h,\phi)})\Bigr\}\biggr),
\end{aligned}
\end{equation}
where the expectation on the right is with respect to the law of~$Z_t$. The measure $Z_t$ obeys \eqref{E:1.13},
$\nu$ is concentrated on~$\{\phi_0=0\}\cap
\bigcap_{x\in\N\smallsetminus \{0\}}\{\phi_x>0\}$ and the set $\{x\in\N\colon \phi_x\le a\}$ is finite~$\nu$-a.s.\ for each~$a>0$. A.e.\ sample of~$Z_t$ is diffuse (i.e., does not charge singletons). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Theorem theorem_localized_eigenvector_localization of arXiv:2504.00512, 'Localization-delocalization transition for a random block matrix model at the edge'] Under (main_assm of the paper), given any $k\in[\![{1,DN}]\!]$, suppose there exists a positive constant $\varepsilon_A$ such that
\begin{equation}
\|A\|_{\text{\rm{HS}}}\le N^{1/3-\varepsilon_A}{\mathfrak{r}}\left({k}\right)^{-1/3} . 
\end{equation}
Then, for any small constant $\varepsilon\in(0,2{\varepsilon}_A)$, there exists a constant $\varepsilon_0=\varepsilon_0\left({\varepsilon}\right)>0$ such that
\begin{equation}\nonumber
    \begin{aligned}
        \mathbb P\left(\max_{a=1}^D \|E_a{\bf v}_k\|^2 \le 1 - N^{-2/3+\varepsilon}{\mathfrak{r}}\left({k}\right)^{2/3}\left\lVert A \right\rVert_{\text{\rm{HS}}}^2\right)\le N^{-\varepsilon_0}.
    \end{aligned}
\end{equation}
As a consequence, it implies that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb P\left(\max_{a=1}^D \|E_a{\bf v}_k\|^2 \le 1 - N^{-c}\right)\le N^{-c}
\end{equation}
for a constant $c>0$ depending on ${\varepsilon}_A$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

