[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $\varepsilon>0$ and $n\in \N$. Consider the rectangles 
$$\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}^{i,j}_{\varepsilon}=\Big[\frac{j-1}{16},\frac{j+1}{16}\Big]\times [(i-1)\varepsilon,i\varepsilon]$$ 
for $j\in \Z$ and $i \in \lbr \varepsilon^{-1}\rbr$, and define the events
 \begin{equation*}
     \mathsf{E}^{i,j}_{n,\varepsilon} :=\left\{ |\Lpat(x,s;y,t)|\leq  \log^{4/3}(\varepsilon^{-1}) \text{ for all } (x,s;y,t) \in (\widetilde{\mathcal{R}}^{i,j}_{\varepsilon})^2_{\uparrow}\cap \mathcal{D}_{\varepsilon} \right\} . 
\end{equation*} 
There exist $c,C>0$ such that for all $\varepsilon>0$ and all $n\in \N$ with $n \geq \varepsilon^{-2}$, 
\begin{equation}
    \P\bigg( \mathsf{E}^{i,j}_{n,\varepsilon} \text{ holds for all } i \in \lbr \varepsilon^{-1}\rbr \text{ and } j\in \Z\bigg) \geq 1- C \varepsilon^{-1}\exp\big(-c \varepsilon^{-1/2}\big). 
\end{equation}

