[Lemma sub-gaussian_cts_quasi of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] Let $G$ be a quasi-transitive graph of polynomial growth. Then, there exist constants $c_{1},c_{2},C_{1},C_{2}>0$ depending on $G$ such that
\begin{equation}
  \frac{c_{1}}{t^{d/2}} e^{-d_{G}^{2}(x,y)/c_{2}t} \leq p_{t}(x,y) \leq \frac{C_{1}}{t^{d/2}} e^{-d_{G}^{2}(x,y)/C_{2}t}
\end{equation}
for all $x,y \in V, t\geq 1$ with $d_{G}(x,y) \leq t$.

