[Proposition 3 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Under Assumption \ref{assumption}, it holds that 
    \begin{align}
        \limsup\limits_{T \to +\infty} \exp(\lambda_1 T)\chi^2(\mu_{T/2}^{T}||\diffref) &\leq 2(K^2+1)\sum_{i\in \mathcal{I}_1} (p_i^2 + q_i^2),
    \end{align}
    where $K = \sup\limits_{T \geq T^*} \norm{b^{T}}_{L^{\infty}(\diffref)}$ for some $T^* > 0$ chosen large enough, guaranteed to exist by \eqref{eq:uniform-bdd-potents}.

