[Lemma lem:process_continuity of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The process $X^a$ is almost surely continuous in the sense that
	\begin{equation*}
		\mathbb{P}_z[X_t^a \in [C_0] \text{ for a.e. } t\in [0,\infty)] = 1 \quad\text{for all } z\inL.
	\end{equation*}
	The same statement holds for $\mathcal{E}$-q.e.\ $z\inL$ for $X$.

[Theorem thm:lsi of arXiv:2510.22778, 'Free denoising diffusion models'] For every $\mu$ with finite second moment and $\Phi^{*}(\mu)<\infty$,
\begin{align}
  \mathcal{D}(\mu\Vert\gamma)&\le\tfrac12\,I(\mu\Vert\gamma), \\
  W_{2}(\mu,\gamma)^{2}&\le 2\,\mathcal{D}(\mu\Vert\gamma). 
\end{align}
Both are sharp, with equality if and only if $\mu=\gamma$.

