[Proposition p:wagestable of arXiv:2604.03979, 'Stationary Distributions in Monotone Markov Models: Theory and Applications'] If (a:quqe of the paper) holds, then the wage process is globally stable, with
    unique stationary distribution $\phi^*$.  Moreover,

    \begin{equation}
        \beta(\phi P_t, \phi^*) \leq C e^{-\alpha t}
        \quad \text{for all } \phi \in \mathscr{P}(S) \text{ and } t \geq 0,
    \end{equation}

    where 

    \begin{equation}
        C \coloneq 2/(1-\kappa), 
        \quad
        \alpha \coloneq \ln(1/(1-\kappa)),
        \quad \text{and} \quad
        \kappa \coloneq \frac{e^{-(\delta + \lambda)} (\delta \wedge \lambda)^n}{n!} \epsilon.
    \end{equation}

[Lem prop:Q:mathcal:N of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix a   continuous function $h:\mathbb{R}_+\to \mathbb{R}_+$ satisfying  $\sigma_h \in(0, \infty)$, with $h(0) = h(\sigma_h) = 0$ and set  $h_{\sigma_h \shortminus \hspace{0,2mm}  \mathpalette\mathpalette\bigcdot@{.5}@{.5}}:= (h((\sigma_h - t)\vee 0) : t\geq 0)$. The following properties hold: 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item[\emph{(i)}] The distribution of $(\overline{W}_{(\sigma_h - t)\vee 0} :  t \geq 0 )$ under $\mathbf{Q}^h_{x,r}$ coincides with the law of  
    $(\overline{W}_{t} : t\geq 0)$ under $\mathbf{Q}^{h_{\sigma_h \shortminus \hspace{0,2mm}  \mathpalette\mathpalette\bigcdot@{.5}@{.5}}}_{x,r}$.  
    \item[\emph{(ii)}] Let $q>0$ be as in (continuity_snake_2 of the paper).  If   $h$ is $\theta$-Hölder-continuous  with $\theta q > 1$,   the canonical process $\overline{W}$ under $\mathbf{Q}_{x,r}^h$ possesses a continuous modification. 
\end{enumerate}

