body:
[Lemma 8 (Absolute inner shadowing) of arXiv:2609.02788, '\textbf{Quantized Einstein Metrics on \(S^7\) with \(SU(3)\)-Symmetry}'] For $s_0$ fixed sufficiently far inside the cone chart,
\begin{equation}
 \|U_{\PE}(s)-U_{\RF}(s)\|\le Cb^2e^{2s},
 \qquad s_0\le s\le s_b,
\end{equation}
uniformly for $|\mu|\le\mu_0$.

[Definition def:UT of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] A line ensemble $\mathbf{X}$ is uniformly tight if for any $\varepsilon > 0$ there is some $C$ such that,
for all $t \in \mathbb{R}$ we have
\begin{equation}
    \mathbb{P} \mleft[X^1(t) \geqslant C\mright] \leqslant \varepsilon.
\end{equation}

[Theorem 4 (High-probability quantile regret of \UCBBQRL) of arXiv:2608.22227, '\fontsize{18pt}{20pt}\selectfont \bf Risk-Sensitive Reinforcement Learning with Smoothed Q'] Let \(\{\beta_t\}_{t\ge0}\subset(0,\tau]\) be non-increasing. Then, for
\UCBBQRL\space with confidence radii in
Equation~\eqref{eq:confset}, with probability at least \(1-2\delta\), $\Reg_\tau(T)
\le\;
2\sum_{t=0}^{T-1}\Delta_{\beta_t} +
\frac{c}{\beta_{T-1}}
\sqrt{SATH^4\log\!\frac{2SATH}{\delta}}
+
\frac{c}{\beta_{T-1}}
\sqrt{
\frac{TH^4}{2}\log\!\frac{2SATH}{\delta}
\log\!\frac{1}{\delta}
}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

