[Lemma lem:Hada of arXiv:2509.02074, 'On the Kolmogorov-Feller weak law of large numbers for the Fr\'{e}chet mean on non-compact'] Suppose that $(M,d)$ is a Hadamard manifold. For any $x,x_1, x_2,\ldots,x_n \in M$, 
\begin{equation}
\|\mbox{Log}_{x}(\mu_{n}) \|_{x} \le  \|\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mbox{Log}_{x}(x_i) \|_{x},
\end{equation}
where $\mu_{n}$ denotes the sample Fr\'{e}chet\ mean of $(x_1, x_2, \ldots x_n) \in M^n$, and $\|\cdot\|_{x}$ denotes the Riemannian norm induced by the Riemannian metric $\langle ~,~\rangle_{x}$ on $T_{x}M$. The inequality in ((ineq:key of the paper)) is strict unless $x,x_1,…,x_n$ all lie in a single totally geodesic flat submanifold of $M$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

